# XCU 1.6 Built-In Utilities
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Utilities that a shell may build in must also exist as files reachable by
# a PATH search and by the exec functions.

assertion  XCU.1.6-built-in-utilities.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap01.html#1.6/regardless of whether they are also implemented as regular built-ins
class      required
since      1992
says       Each standard utility that is neither a special built-in nor an
           intrinsic utility (except kill, which is one) exists as an executable
           file found by a search of PATH, and the file runs when named by its
           path: echo, printf, true, false, test, [, kill, basename, dirname and
           expr give their expected results.
timeout    60
test       t/001-exec-reachable.sh

assertion  XCU.1.6-built-in-utilities.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap01.html#1.6/exec
class      required
since      1992
says       Utilities that run other utilities (env, xargs, find -exec, and nohup,
           nice and time where present) can run echo, printf, true, test, kill,
           basename, dirname and expr, and false gives status 1 through env.
timeout    60
test       t/002-run-by-utilities.sh
